.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWN-PRESENCE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clown-presence
.Nd query the clown session presence index
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm clown presence list
.Op Fl -group Ar group-id
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -quiet
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm clown presence
queries the presence index \(em the clown\(->spinclass liveness seam (RFC-0014).
The index is kept by ringmaster's host service (see
.Xr ringmaster 1 ) .
Every live clown announces itself at launch for a two-minute window, and stays
present for as long as its wake monitor's subscription lives; a session that
does neither within the window drops out.
This command is the stable query surface for that index: a consumer \(em notably
spinclass's liveness probe \(em uses it instead of asking the service directly,
so the record schema and the freshness window stay clown's concern.
It is a pure read, and fails when the host service cannot be reached.
.Pp
A clown is present only if it announces itself or its job-watch monitor is running:
the claude-family providers, not
.Fl -naked
or an exec-replacing provider, and not when
.Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_JOB_WAKEUP Ns = Ns Ql 1 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Nm clown presence list
List the live presence records.
By default the output is a human listing grouped by
.Sy decoration
(the group-id), each line showing a record's per-instance key and description \(em
the same shape as
.Nm clown chat list .
.Fl -group
restricts the listing to records whose
.Sy decoration
.Pq the group-id, Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID , No e.g. a spinclass session's Ar repo Ns / Ns Ar branch
equals
.Ar group-id ;
passing
.Fl -group
with an empty value selects the ungrouped records.
.Fl -json
emits one JSON record per line
.Pq Li {sessionKey,channelId,decoration,description,lastSeen} .
.Fl -quiet
suppresses output and turns the command into a liveness predicate: it exits
.Sy 0
when at least one matching live record exists and
.Sy 1
when none do
.Pq Xr grep 1 Fl q No style ,
so a probe is
.Dl clown presence list --group \(dq$ID\(dq --quiet
.El
.Sh SESSION KEY AND REATTACH
The
.Sy sessionKey
field is the record's per-instance routing key (RFC-0013 §2).
For a claude-family session it is the very same value as the
.Ql posh
multiplexer session the worker runs under, the claude
.Fl -session-id ,
and the
.Ql session_id
a SessionStart hook receives \(em all the one freshly minted UUID clown resolves
per instance (RFC-0013 §2.1).
.Pp
That identity is what lets an orchestrator reattach a worker it launched
detached \(em the spawn wire of RFC-0014 §5, e.g.\& spinclass's
.Ic sc spawn .
clown mints the id, names the detached
.Ql posh
session by it, and records it here, so the live session is addressable as
.Sy sessionKey
without the worker reporting anything back:
.Dl name=$(clown presence list --group \(dq$GROUP\(dq --json | jq -r .sessionKey)
.Dl posh attach \(dq$name\(dq
.Pp
When more than one live worker shares a
.Ar group-id ,
.Fl -group
returns every member and a freshly spawned worker is not distinguishable from its
siblings in the listing alone; the launcher must then correlate the spawn it made
to a
.Sy sessionKey
by other means (for example the worker reporting its own
.Ql session_id
back at startup).
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Where the host service's socket lives
.Pq Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ringmaster/service.sock .
.It Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID
The group-id a live clown records as its
.Sy decoration ;
.Fl -group
matches against it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm clown presence list
exits
.Sy 0
on success
.Pq or, with Fl -quiet , No when a matching record is live ,
.Sy 1
on a read error
.Pq or, with Fl -quiet , No when no matching record is live ,
and
.Sy 2
on a usage error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ringmaster 1 ,
.Xr troupe 1 ,
.Xr clownfile 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC-0014 (clown\(enspinclass awareness seam: group-id and presence) and RFC-0013
(clownfile, per-instance identity, and clown-owned chat).
